  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xF6;d till IPS Communication Foundation 2024-2027</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to IPS Communication Foundation 2024-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention&apos;s intended impact is a stronger and broader defense for a free, critical and pluralistic media in T&#xFC;rkiye.
The intervention will strive towards this impact through the following outcomes:
1) Readers and stakeholders in T&#xFC;rkiye continue to receive accurate and rights-oriented news 
2) Journalists who adhere to universal values engage in rights-oriented journalism
3) Evidence-based work of advocates for freedom of expression and a conducive environment for the press strengthened
4) Civil society, academia and independent press are restoring their ties through rights journalism
5) IPS more resilient, more participatory, more sustainable</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">M&#xE5;len f&#xF6;r insatsen &#xE4;r:
1) L&#xE4;sare och intressenter i Turkiet forts&#xE4;tter att f&#xE5; korrekta och r&#xE4;ttighetsbaserade nyheter fr&#xE5;n Bianet och kan d&#xE4;rmed mobilisera sig f&#xF6;r
r&#xE4;ttigheter, demokrati och r&#xE4;ttsstatens principer
2) Journalister som arbetar enligt universella v&#xE4;rden (inklusive nya former av journalistik) engagerar sig i r&#xE4;ttighetsbaserad journalistik
3) St&#xE4;rkt gynnsam milj&#xF6; f&#xF6;r media och st&#xE4;rkt evidensbaserat arbete bland f&#xF6;respr&#xE5;kare f&#xF6;r yttrandefrihet
4) Civilsamh&#xE4;llet, den akademiska v&#xE4;rlden och oberoende media (lokal, nationell, regional och internationell) st&#xE4;rker sitt samarbete inom
r&#xE4;ttighetsbaserad journalistik f&#xF6;r arbete inom m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter
5) IPS &#xE4;r mer motst&#xE5;ndskraftigt, mer delaktigt och mer h&#xE5;llbart</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives of the intervention are the following:
 1) Readers and stakeholders in Turkey continue to receive accurate and rights-oriented news from Bianet and are thus able to mobilize for rights, democracy and the rule of law
 2) Journalists who adhere to universal values (including new forms of journalism) engage in rights &#xAD;oriented journalism
 3) Evidence &#xAD;based work of advocates for freedom of expression and a conducive environment for the press strengthened
 4) Civil society, academia and independent press (local, national, regional and international) are restoring their ties in the forefront of the struggle for rights through rights journalism
 5) IPS more resilient, more participatory, more sustainable</narrative>
  </description>
